# The three-protocol image (firmware/examples/multi.asm), thread 0: the WS2812 waveform, with the same checks as
# ws2812.timing. The code is the stand-alone driver's; this spec proves that in this image, where threads 2 and 3
# run an I2C target and a UART at the same time, the waveform is still exactly the same (a thread's timing depends
# only on its own instructions: docs/verification.md, the isolation proofs).
program ../examples/multi.asm
thread 0
start ws_next
nonblocking
init A=? X=? C=?
event RISE = at ws_bit
event FALL = out 2=0

check RISE -> FALL in [250ns, 550ns] [650ns, 950ns]     # T0H or T1H
check FALL -> RISE in [300ns, 600ns] [700ns, 1000ns]    # T1L or T0L
check RISE -> RISE == 1.28us                             # every bit the same length, even across a byte boundary
